{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/295844-recruiting-vtr-b-s-demo-game-even-for-people-without-the-books","id":295844,"title":"[Recruiting][VtR/B&S]Demo game even for people without the books","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-29T07:45:27-07:00","id":295844,"title":"[Recruiting][VtR/B&S]Demo game even for people without the books","content":"Short version: Interested in trying out Vampire the Requiem with newest rules? This is your chance, no book required! One game can take 4-5 players, but I can run several if there's interest.<br /> <br /> <b>System</b><br /> New World of Darkness 2nd edition (God Machine Chronicle), Vampire the Requiem 2nd edition (Blood &amp; Smoke: The Strix Chronicle).<br /> <br /> <b>Setting</b><br /> Demo SAS Dance de la Mort; a story of five just embraced fledlings. The demo rules and GMC update are available online. The characters are pregenerated, so you only need to handle the game play parts.<br /> <br /> The characters are Louis Maddox, a computer geek/knowledge bank; Tina Baker, a pretty brawler; Becky Lynn Adler, a really pretty social type; Jack McCandless, a driver/man of the street; and joining in the second session Edward Zuric, an inspiring musician. Conveniently all getting embraced to different clans... You can read more about the characters on pages 19-23 and 58 of <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/produc...Demo-Full?it=1\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/produc...Demo-Full?it=1</a>. It also has some rules at the beginning of every session, but they are using the first edition of VtR. I will convert the setting, including the characters, to the latest rules. Reading more of the demo will spoil the game for you.<br /> <br /> The demo itself already gives the fledlings three dots of predecided disciplines, but I find that a bit boring and unnecessary. I think it should be reasonable for the characters to gradually find their capabilities.<br /> <br /> Tina and Jack are already reserved for the first game.<br /> <br /> <b>Player requirements</b><br /> The story works for four or five people who haven't read the demo before, perhaps best if you don't have much or any experience with VtR at all. There are two players already interested, so minimum of two more is required. If there's a lot of interest, I can run many games.<br /> <br /> The only prerequisites are decent skills in English and commitment to participate every day most days, even if it's just a one liner in busy days. After 48 hours of absence the PC acts with ST fiat, unless the player has announced his leave. Preferably another player would handle that PC in the meantime, but I won't force it. If a player seems to disappear completely (say a week of silence) I'll make the PC an NPC, unless there are players wanting to join midgame.<br /> <br /> You don't need any books; the GMC rule update is at <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/114078/World-of-Darkness-GodMachine-Rules-Update\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/produc...e-Rules-Update</a> and the demo itself covers the rest.<br /> <br /> <b>Gaming medium</b><br /> Preferably IRC, but I'm skeptical of finding a time slot that works for all, so play by post or email is the likeliest choice. Forum can be at giantitp, though the dice roller doesn't really offer much and there are no target tags for posting part of content to certain players. Pure PbP forums could be ok too, but I don't have first hand experience of those. Suggestions are welcome. Working email notifications are a must-have feature for me, thus the Onyx Path forum won't work, unfortunately.<br /> <br /> The medium also affects the game style. Unless we can manage a real time chat game, I'll keep combat pretty simple so it doesn't last forever. There won't be much of puzzles, so the game will be mostly roleplay oriented.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice rolling</b><br /> I think it should be ok for PCs to roll their own unopposed rolls with forum roller, so that the next player knows what happens if I haven't visited the thread in between yet. If the difficulty wasn't correct, I'll just select the right number of dice starting from left. For opposed rolls and those I'm calling (especially for multiple chars) I'll make the roll immediately.<br /> <br /> Player rolls are honored, but if an NPC makes a completely story breaking roll with implausible number of explosions (think headshot from a mile away or so), I'll veto it. If there's a player roll where one outcome would result in a significantly more fun game/story, I'll just skip the roll and directly call the result. Though if the player knowingly does something very risky, there's no mercy. This applies more to situations that belong to the plot.<br /> <br /> It's an open question to the players do they want to know about roll results which wouldn't realistically give any feedback on success (perception, bluffing etc.), and whether they want to know about roll results that are not IC knowledge for all PCs.<br /> <br /> <br /> Please ask for more info here, or via PM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4014-hukka","name":"hukka","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}